<http://www.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/event/34401AVSCHHTDLGCSLVJRSQLBPTLHDKLB>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "In Conversation: Donna Morrissey (In Person)";
  schema:description """
	<img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/d5a19351-660f-4b69-bfa8-f6bf2939d9e7.jpg\" /><span><br/></span><h1>In Conversation with Donna Morrissey</h1><span><br/></span>Join our host Liz Crocker as she sits down in conversation with award-winning author Donna Morrissey to discuss her newly released memoir <span class=\"ItalicText\">Tell It to the Water</span>.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Donna's memoir of her father's approaching death is a raucous hymn to family life--the ties that enthrall, enrage and bind you, if only in your heart, to the place that will always be home because it's where Mom and Dad set your wobbly feet on the ground.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Heartbreak meets rip-roaring humor as Donna and her siblings share stories of the dad they're about to lose--the Newfoundland version of a Greek chorus. You can practically smell the sea and feel the Ski-Doo  tearing through the woods, but this is a universal tale. If you've ever mourned a parent, especially one who drove you nuts, this fractured but defiantly devoted family is singing your song.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Among Donna’s writing honours are the Thomas Raddall Atlantic Fiction Award and the Arthur Ellis Award for Best Crime Fiction for <span class=\"ItalicText\">The Fortunate Brother</span>; <span class=\"ItalicText\">Sylvanus Now</span> was shortlisted for the Commonwealth Writers’ Prize; and <span class=\"ItalicText\">The Deception of Livvy Higgs</span> was a One Read pick for Nova Scotia in 2017. Her fiction has also won awards in the US and the UK, and has been translated into several languages. Born and raised in Newfoundland, she lives in Halifax.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>We are thrilled to welcome Donna to the Chester Playhouse once again, and hope you can join us for what is bound to be a heartfelt, entertaining afternoon.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Copies of <span class=\"ItalicText\">Tell It to the Water</span> will be available for sale at the event courtesy of our friends Village Emporium.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Can’t join us in person? We are pleased to also offer this in conversation via Livestream. Purchase a <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://purchase.chesterplayhouse.ca/ChooseSeats/
34601/\">livestream ticket</a>, and watch the event live, or for one week following the event!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">When</span> <span><br/></span>Sunday, November 22nd at 2pm<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">75 minutes, no intermission</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tickets</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Adults</span> - <span class=\"BoldText\">$20.00</span>  ($14.92 + taxes & $3 Building Reserve Fee)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Youth (4-19)</span> - <span class=\"BoldText\">$10 </span> ($6.14 + taxes & $3 Building Reserve Fee) <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>General Admission Seating<span><br/></span>Doors open 45mins before the show.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The Chester Playhouse is wheelchair accessible. Please call the Box Office at (902) 275-3933 to arrange accessible seating.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Babes in arms & children under 4 are not permitted in the theatre.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-11-22T14:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/d5a19351-660f-4b69-bfa8-f6bf2939d9e7.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/location/601APNNMRMBJQQPBSCNQGQHGKKCRPSSGN>;
  schema:offers _:98c7b39533524a8098b484e4a7b4c9fd5;
