<http://www.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/event/26601APLTNSPSGDPBRQVGGSRDMVBVVNQK>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "James Mullinger";
  schema:description """
	<img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/682c4c09-6dad-47bb-ab99-d2435835f1f9.jpg\" /><span><br/></span><h1>James Mullinger</h1><h2>Canadian Comedian</h2><span><br/></span>A Chester favourite stand up comedian, <span class=\"BoldText\">James Mullinger</span> returns for hilarious observations on Maritime life.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Award-winning comedian James Mullinger is embarking on his biggest cross-Canada tour yet with his brand new stand-up show Canadian Comedian - a hilarious and heartfelt love letter to his adopted home.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Having moved from London, England to New Brunswick, Canada over a decade ago, James has become one of Canada’s most celebrated comedians, selling out arenas and theatres across the country. Canadian Comedian explores everything James adores about Canada - small-town life in the Maritimes, the kindness of Canadians, and the quirks that make this the greatest country in the world. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The show also sees James at his most personal, sharing stories about parenting, being diagnosed with ADHD later in life, his citizenship ceremony, and finding joy (and comedy) in the chaos of everyday life and what it means to be a Canadian by choice.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>This is James’ first show in Chester for two years and he can’t wait to return! Book now - he always sells out fast! <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>“<span class=\"ItalicText\">Comedian James Mullinger has the audience laughing uproariously</span>.” - The Globe & Mail<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>“<span class=\"ItalicText\">Unmissable</span>.” -GQ Magazine<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>“<span class=\"ItalicText\">A great stand up</span>.” -Jimmy Carr<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4UfglK-YnUk?si=o5JvqgBhGTCdVxTG\">Discover James Mullinger!</a><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">When</span> <span><br/></span>Saturday, November 7th at 7:30 pm<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">75 minutes, no intermission</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tickets</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Adults</span> - <span class=\"BoldText\">$42.00</span>  ($42.99 + taxes & $3 Building Reserve Fee)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Youth (4-19)</span> - <span class=\"BoldText\">$26.00 </span> ($20.18 + taxes & $3 Building Reserve Fee) <span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">$10 Community Tickets</span> use code <span class=\"BoldText\">10FOR10</span> (<span class=\"ItalicText\">limit of 10 per performance</span>)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Reserved Seating<span><br/></span>Doors open 45mins before the show.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The Chester Playhouse is wheelchair accessible. Please call the Box Office at (902) 275-3933 to arrange accessible seating.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Babes in arms & children under 4 are not permitted in the theatre.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-11-07T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
