  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "On This Winter's Night ";
  schema:description """
	<img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/0657cfce-d3b6-420e-ac1f-b2e6dcf83d62.jpg\" /><span><br/></span><h1>Tara MacLean and The Bayfield String Quartet</h1><span><br/></span>Curl up for <span class=\"ItalicText\">On This Winter’s Night</span>, a cozy and elegant evening of glistening winter music and storytelling with one of Canada’s foremost award-winning vocalists and best selling author, Tara MacLean. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Joined by the Bayfield String Quartet, Tara will share a luminous blend of classic, contemporary, and original songs, curating an unforgettable night. Through song and story, <span class=\"ItalicText\">On This Winter’s Night</span> will wrap the audience in the magic of the season — weaving warmth, wonder, and holiday spirit into every heart.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>About Tara MacLean:<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Canadian singer/songwriter Tara MacLean has been an internationally renowned and award winning recording and touring artist for over 25 years. She released her first album with the Nettwerk Music Group in 1996 and Sony Music Publishing Canada. Since then has been signed with Capitol Records, and EMI Canada with her JUNO nominated band Shaye. She has written and recorded seven solo albums and two with the band.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Tara won the Contemporary Roots Recording of the Year award at the 2025 Music PEI awards for her <span class=\"ItalicText\">Live in My Hometown</span> EP. In 2024, she received three nominations for her album <span class=\"ItalicText\">Sparrow</span> at the East Coast Music Awards, and took home the award for Single of the Year at the MPEI Awards. Last year, Tara received the Stompin' Tom award by the East Coast Music Association, marking an outstanding contribution to music in the region.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>About the Bayfield String Quartet:<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The Bayfield String Quartet, known for their vibrant and engaging performances, is a dynamic ensemble that brings a fresh perspective to the string quartet tradition. Comprising four exceptional musicians—Karen Graves (violin), Kinley Dowling (violin), Jeffrey Bazett-Jones (viola), and Natalie Williams Calhoun (cello)—the quartet has quickly established itself in Charlottetown as one of the most compelling ensembles on the local chamber music scene. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://youtube.com/watch?v=jyO5HxhAbGg&amp;feature=youtu.be/\">Watch the Trailer!</a><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">When</span> <span><br/></span>Saturday, November 28th at 7:30 pm<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">2x45 minute sets, plus intermission</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tickets</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Adults</span> - <span class=\"BoldText\">$55.00</span>  ($45.62 + taxes & $3 Building Reserve Fee)<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Youth (4-19)</span> - <span class=\"BoldText\">$27.50 </span> ($21.50 + taxes & $3 Building Reserve Fee) <span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">$10 Community Tickets</span> use code <span class=\"BoldText\">10FOR10</span> (<span class=\"ItalicText\">limit of 10 per performance</span>)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Reserved Seating<span><br/></span>Doors open 45mins before the show.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The Chester Playhouse is wheelchair accessible. Please call the Box Office at (902) 275-3933 to arrange accessible seating.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Babes in arms & children under 4 are not permitted in the theatre.<span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-11-28T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
