<http://www.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/event/32401ANQMVQVNTGTQHTSGSGJCPVKHDGKP>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Silent Night (MET Opera)";
  schema:description """
	<img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/e86f172d-49dc-4443-b7e3-df98461bcd58.jpg\" /><span><br/></span><h1>Silent Night</h1><h2>MET Opera Live in HD (Encore)</h2><span><br/></span>Following his smash-hit company debut with <span class=\"ItalicText\">The Hours</span>, composer Kevin Puts returns to the Met with his Pulitzer Prize–winning first opera, <span class=\"ItalicText\">Silent Night</span>.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Inspired by the true events of the 1914 Christmas truce, <span class=\"ItalicText\">Silent Night</span> takes us to the moment when soldiers spontaneously set aside the horrors of the First World War and crossed the trenches to mingle, exchange gifts, and sing carols with the enemy.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>A poignant depiction of shared humanity in the most inhumane circumstances, Puts’s grand, cinematic opera—with a libretto by Mark Campbell based on the film <span class=\"ItalicText\">Joyeux Noël</span> —has been widely acclaimed since its 2011 premiere, hailed as “an overwhelming emotive experience” by The Guardian. <span class=\"ItalicText\">Silent Night</span> receives an evocative staging by James Robinson that takes the audience directly to the battlefields of the Western Front. The star-studded cast, featuring soprano Elza van den Heever and tenors Ben Bliss and Rolando Villazón, among many others, is conducted by debuting maestro Dalia Stasevska.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">When</span> <span><br/></span>Sunday, May 16th at 2:00 pm<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Runtime - TBC</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tickets</span><span><br/></span>Adults -<span class=\"BoldText\">$23.00</span> ($17.54+ tax & $3 Building Reserve Fee)<span><br/></span>Youth (under 20) -<span class=\"BoldText\">$11.50</span>  ($7.45 + tax & $3 Building Reserve Fee) <span><br/></span>$10 Community Tickets use code <span class=\"BoldText\">10FOR10</span> (<span class=\"ItalicText\">limit of 10 per performance</span>)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Genre: Opera<span><br/></span>Language: Sung in French with English subtitles<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Admission includes complimentary popcorn.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>General Admission<span><br/></span>Doors open 45 mins before the show.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The Chester Playhouse is wheelchair accessible. Please call the Box Office at (902) 275-3933 to arrange accessible seating.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Babes in arms & children under 4 are not permitted in the theatre.<span><br/></span>
""";
