  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Tony";
  schema:description """
	<img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/chesterplayhousenovascotia/files/255dff6e-ab77-48d8-b108-ffefc53ce0b6.jpg\" /><span><br/></span><h1>Tony</h1><span><br/></span>Canadian director Matt Johnson (<span class=\"ItalicText\">Nirvanna, The Band, The Show, The Movie</span>) brings the extraordinary story of iconic chef, author, and broadcaster Anthony Bourdain to the big screen with <span class=\"ItalicText\">Tony</span>.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Synopsis</span>:<span><br/></span>In this origin story of a voice that defined a generation, 19-year-old Anthony Bourdain (portrayed by Dominic Sessa, the breakout star from <span class=\"ItalicText\">The Holdovers</span>) stumbles into the chaotic world of a Cape Cod restaurant kitchen, setting off a summer that will shape the course of his life.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Tony currently sits with a 93% Fresh resting on RottenTomatoes.com with critics raving:<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>“<span class=\"ItalicText\">Before he was \"Anthony Bourdain,\" he was just Tony, carrying raw kitchen confidential experiences with a flame to venture into parts unknown. \"Tony\" is a briny, consequential coming-of-age story, seasoned with a blend of authenticity, chaos and care</span>.” - The MovieMaven<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>“<span class=\"ItalicText\">Sessa captures Bourdain’s sardonic wit, and his performance hints at the evolution of the Anthony Bourdain we know from his writing and shows: a person who used self-deprecating humor to mock his flaws and career</span>.” - Fort Worth Report<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k1MVnzd2aVc/\">Watch the Trailer!</a><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">When</span> <span><br/></span>Sunday, November 15th at 2:00 pm<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">1 hour and 46 minutes</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tickets</span><span><br/></span>Adults -<span class=\"BoldText\">$17.00</span> ($12.28+ tax & $3 Building Reserve Fee)<span><br/></span>Youth (18-19) -<span class=\"BoldText\">$9</span>  ($5.26 + tax & $3 Building Reserve Fee) <span><br/></span>$10 Community Tickets use code <span class=\"BoldText\">10FOR10</span> (<span class=\"ItalicText\">limit of 10 per performance</span>)<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Rating: R (Language, Sexual Content, Nudity)<span><br/></span>Genre: Drama/Biography<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Admission includes complimentary popcorn.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>General Admission<span><br/></span>Doors open 45 mins before the show.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The Chester Playhouse is wheelchair accessible. Please call the Box Office at (902) 275-3933 to arrange accessible seating.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Babes in arms & children under 4 are not permitted in the theatre.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>
""";
